{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of the pair-graph regime trichotomy","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-pair-graph-regime-trichotomy"],"text":"pair-graph-regime-trichotomy-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:pair-graph-regime-trichotomy\"></a><p>By Pascal's rule <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom{n+1}2 = n+\\binom n2</code>, so by induction <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2\\binom A2 = A(A-1)</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb Z</code>. Hence</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">2\\tbinom A2-2(3A-6) = A^2-7A+12 = (A-3)(A-4).</code></pre>\n<p>The right side is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=3,4</code> and at least <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2=3A-6</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\in\\{3,4\\}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2>3A-6</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code>. Also <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A3=0</code> if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A&#x3C;3</code>. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge2</code> the cases <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\in\\{3,4\\}</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code> are exhaustive and disjoint, which gives the trichotomy. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa</code>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(2)=1=\\binom22</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(3)=3=\\binom32</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(4)=6=\\binom42</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(A)=3A-6&#x3C;\\binom A2</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code>.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\blacksquare</code></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pair-graph-regime-trichotomy-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","qa":{"counts":{"pass":1,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":0,"unknown":0,"stale":0}}}
